@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Our Journey";
}

<div class="container py-5">

    <!-- Page Header -->
    <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <h1 class="fw-bold glow-text display-5">Project Journey</h1>
        <p class="lead">The chronological evolution, milestones, and breakthroughs behind InvestorVirtual.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-5">

        <!-- ROW 1: Text Left, Image Right -->
        <div class="row align-items-center g-4">
            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="terminal-card rounded-4 p-4 shadow-sm h-100 d-flex flex-column justify-content-center">
                    <h3 class="fw-bold glow-text mb-3">Weird and unexpected guest</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
                        Using the skills acquired by the years in 2D vector desing I decided to add a touch of something personal so I used CorelDrawX7 to bring these vector variants of company logos to life for my own use for this project.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-6 text-center">
                <img src="~/images/journey/journey1.jpg" alt="Journey Milestone 1" class="img-fluid rounded-4 shadow-lg w-100 journey-img" style="max-height: 380px; object-fit: cover; transition: transform 0.35s ease-in-out;" onmouseover="this.style.transform='scale(1.03)'" onmouseout="this.style.transform='scale(1)'" />
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ROW 2: Image Left, Text Right (Zig-Zag) -->
        <div class="row align-items-center g-4 flex-lg-row-reverse">
            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="terminal-card rounded-4 p-4 shadow-sm h-100 d-flex flex-column justify-content-center">
                    <h3 class="fw-bold glow-text mb-3">The source site</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
                        Even though I could have ran with completely fabricated data for the sake of the simulation (which at this time is not operational) I decided to look-up and use exact information regarding parts of the information about stocks (like prices at a certain date, sectors, descriptions, exact names, etc.) Most likely, if I knew already how to pull historical analysies or had the patience to read through news, I would've taken them as well.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-6 text-center">
                <img src="~/images/journey/journey2.png" alt="Journey Milestone 2" class="img-fluid rounded-4 shadow-lg w-100 journey-img" style="max-height: 380px; object-fit: cover; transition: transform 0.35s ease-in-out;" onmouseover="this.style.transform='scale(1.03)'" onmouseout="this.style.transform='scale(1)'" />
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ROW 3: Text Left, Image Right -->
        <div class="row align-items-center g-4">
            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="terminal-card rounded-4 p-4 shadow-sm h-100 d-flex flex-column justify-content-center">
                    <h3 class="fw-bold glow-text mb-3">Not perfect...</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
                        While with the mock data used, for the exact date shown in the image, the current price for me is higher than the last (since my data points are between around a month for each milestone)... The actual data shows the opposite and for that particular day the market was bearish.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-6 text-center">
                <img src="~/images/journey/journey3.png" alt="Journey Milestone 3" class="img-fluid rounded-4 shadow-lg w-100 journey-img" style="max-height: 380px; object-fit: cover; transition: transform 0.35s ease-in-out;" onmouseover="this.style.transform='scale(1.03)'" onmouseout="this.style.transform='scale(1)'" />
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ROW 4: Image Left, Text Right (Zig-Zag) -->
        <div class="row align-items-center g-4 flex-lg-row-reverse">
            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="terminal-card rounded-4 p-4 shadow-sm h-100 d-flex flex-column justify-content-center">
                    <h3 class="fw-bold glow-text mb-3">The unexpected fixes</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
                        Forgetting something as simple as how to store paths ended up causing me to have to edit my DB locally on my end so I don't tear it down, while also manually editing the seeding and the migration files as well, so they read paths properly... And I think even then I still broke it by not makin the path start with "~/", or "/"
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-6 text-center">
                <img src="~/images/journey/journey4.png" alt="Journey Milestone 4" class="img-fluid rounded-4 shadow-lg w-100 journey-img" style="max-height: 380px; object-fit: cover; transition: transform 0.35s ease-in-out;" onmouseover="this.style.transform='scale(1.03)'" onmouseout="this.style.transform='scale(1)'" />
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>

<!-- Lightbox Modal Overlay (Hidden by default) -->
<div id="imageLightbox" onclick="this.style.display='none'" style="display:none; position:fixed; top:0; left:0; width:100%; height:100%; background:rgba(0,0,0,0.85); z-index:9999; justify-content:center; align-items:center; cursor:pointer;">
    <img id="lightboxImg" class="img-fluid rounded-4 shadow-lg" style="max-width: 90%; max-height: 90%; object-fit: contain;" />
</div>

@section Scripts {
    <script>
        document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function () {
            const lightbox = document.getElementById('imageLightbox');
            const lightboxImg = document.getElementById('lightboxImg');

            // Attach click event to all journey images
            document.querySelectorAll('.journey-img').forEach(img => {
                img.style.cursor = 'pointer';
                img.addEventListener('click', function () {
                    lightboxImg.src = this.src;
                    lightbox.style.display = 'flex';
                });
            });
        });
    </script>
}